	// Build your receiver to tolerate additive growth, and keep that tolerance
	// separate from the two mechanisms above, which are NOT affected by new fields:
	//
	// - **Validate** only the fields you understand, and ignore the rest — a field
	//   you have never seen is expected, not an error.
	// - **Deduplicate** on the `X-K0r-Event-Source` / `X-K0r-Event-Id` headers (see
	//   "Retries and duplicates"), never on the body's field set.
	// - **Verify the signature** over the entire raw body exactly as received,
	//   including fields you do not recognise (see "Verifying a delivery"). Do not
	//   strip unknown fields before verifying — that changes the bytes and breaks the
	//   signature.
	//
	// ## Network requirements
	//
	// Your endpoint must be reachable from the platform's outbound (egress) network,
	// and deliveries arrive from the platform's egress addresses — not from a fixed
	// address embedded in this API. Those source addresses are a property of the
	// deployment you are integrating with, not of the contract, so if your receiver
	// is behind an allow-list or firewall, get the current egress ranges to permit
	// from your platform operator's networking/deployment guide rather than assuming
	// a value here. There is no inbound connection from you to the platform for
	// delivery — it is one-way, platform → the URL you registered over HTTP(S) (a
	// plaintext `http://` receiver on an internal network is supported; see the `url`
	// field below).
	//
	// Takes a body of the `application/json` content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
	//
	// Corresponds with POST /v1/regions/global/notifications/webhooks (the `CreateWebhookSubscription` operationId).
